// Layer 1 only, no eval/plugin.py, because everything
// that matters here is either a literal string the skill prescribes or a shape the
// skill's own verify.sh already checks. A model judge would add cost and noise
// without adding a measurement.
//
// Both cases seed a folder and grade the file written INTO it. Seeded files are
// collected as artifacts too -- baseline hashing only covers the skill's own source
// -- so every `file_glob` here is an exact path rather than a `*CLAUDE.md` glob.
// Otherwise case 2's regexes would read the seeded ROOT CLAUDE.md and pass on
// content the agent never wrote.
//
// AGENTS.md is deliberately not graded through `file_glob`: it is a symlink, and
// collect_artifacts skips symlinks (sandbox.py:452). The symlink is proved instead by
// `validator_pass_regex`, since verify.sh prints PASS only after resolving it --
// which is also the higher-signal check, because it fails on a copy.
//
// Not covered, and known: the Step 1 gate that declines a folder which does not
// deserve a file. Grading it needs a "no file was produced" grader the kit does not
// have, and a case whose expected outcome is an empty workspace invites the agent to
// stall rather than finish. Add it with the grader, not before.
{
    "id": "claude-md-ingest-folder",
    "prompt": "Write a CLAUDE.md for the ingest/ folder so the next agent working in there has the context it needs.",
    "seed_files": {
        "ingest/README.md": "# ingest\n\nPulls CloudTrail digest files from the `audit-digests` S3 bucket and normalizes\nthem into Parquet under `s3://audit-lake/cloudtrail/`, partitioned for Athena.\n\nRuns as a Lambda behind a 5-minute EventBridge schedule. Not a service; there is\nno API in front of it.\n",
        "ingest/handler.py": "\"\"\"Lambda entrypoint for the digest ingest.\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport os\n\n# Hard cap. Above 500 records the downstream synchronous invoke exceeds the 6 MB\n# Lambda response limit and fails the whole batch, not just the overflow. Raising\n# this has been tried twice.\nBATCH_SIZE = 500\n\nBUCKET = os.environ[\"DIGEST_BUCKET\"]\n\n\ndef handler(event, context):\n    records = _fetch(event)\n    if len(records) > BATCH_SIZE:\n        records = records[:BATCH_SIZE]\n    return {\"written\": _write(records)}\n\n\ndef _fetch(event):\n    return json.loads(event.get(\"body\") or \"[]\")\n\n\ndef _write(records):\n    # Timestamps stay UTC and ISO-8601. Athena partition projection is configured\n    # for dt=YYYY-MM-DD, so a local-time timestamp lands in the wrong partition\n    # silently instead of raising.\n    return len(records)\n",
        "ingest/normalize_cloudtrail.py": "\"\"\"CloudTrail-specific field mapping.\n\nOne module per source, named normalize_<source>.py. normalize_vpcflow.py and\nnormalize_alb.py follow the same shape.\n\"\"\"\n\nFIELDS = [\"eventTime\", \"eventName\", \"userIdentity\", \"sourceIPAddress\"]\n\n\ndef normalize(record):\n    # Every new field must be added as nullable. The Glue crawler runs after this\n    # step, and a non-nullable column breaks backfills of older partitions.\n    return {k: record.get(k) for k in FIELDS}\n",
        "ingest/notes.md": "# notes\n\n2026-04-12 - Parquet over JSONL. Athena scan cost on the standard query set\ndropped roughly 8x. Decided; not open for discussion again.\n\n2026-05-03 - Removed the DynamoDB dedupe table. S3 digest object keys are already\nunique per delivery, so it was paying for a guarantee we already had. Do not\nreintroduce it.\n\n2026-06-20 - Kept the ingest as a Lambda rather than moving to Glue. Runtime is\nunder 40s at p99 and Glue's cold start was worse than the whole invocation.\n\nOpen: whether to backfill 2025 digests at all. Nobody has asked for them yet.\n",
        "ingest/schema.json": "{\n  \"type\": \"record\",\n  \"name\": \"cloudtrail_normalized\",\n  \"fields\": [\n    {\"name\": \"eventTime\", \"type\": [\"null\", \"string\"], \"default\": null},\n    {\"name\": \"eventName\", \"type\": [\"null\", \"string\"], \"default\": null},\n    {\"name\": \"userIdentity\", \"type\": [\"null\", \"string\"], \"default\": null},\n    {\"name\": \"sourceIPAddress\", \"type\": [\"null\", \"string\"], \"default\": null}\n  ]\n}\n"
    },
    "expect": {
        "skill": "folder-specific-claude-and-agents-md",
        "file_glob": "ingest/CLAUDE.md",
        "validator_pass_regex": "PASS: ingest/CLAUDE\\.md",
        "tools_any_order": [
            "Skill",
            "Read",
            "Write",
            "Bash"
        ],
        "tools_in_order": [
            "Skill",
            "Read",
            "Write",
            "Bash"
        ],
        "artifact_regex": [
            "\\b500\\b",
            "(?i)ISO.?8601|\\bUTC\\b",
            "(?i)dedupe|dynamodb",
            "(?i)must not|constraint",
            "(?i)normalize_"
        ],
        "artifact_regex_absent": [
            "[├└│]",
            "(?i)\\bTODO\\b",
            "(?i)\\bplaceholder\\b"
        ],
        "min_counts": {
            "(?m)^##\\s+": 3,
            "(?m)^\\s*[-*]\\s+": 8
        },
        "max_tool_calls": 20,
        "assertions": [
            "Every rule and fact in ingest/CLAUDE.md traces back to the seeded files rather than to generic best practice: the 500-record batch cap and why raising it fails, the UTC / ISO-8601 timestamp requirement tied to Athena partition projection, the nullable-field rule tied to the Glue crawler, and the dated decision not to reintroduce the DynamoDB dedupe table.",
            "Hard prohibitions sit in a Constraints (MUST NOT) section, separate from soft 'usually do X' patterns such as the normalize_<source>.py naming convention, which sit in Conventions.",
            "The file contains no directory tree, no file listing for its own sake, and nothing an agent could derive by running LS or grep in the folder.",
            "Dated decisions from notes.md are recorded as locked decisions with their dates, and the still-open question about backfilling 2025 digests is not presented as decided.",
            "Absolute rules carry their exceptions rather than being stated as bare ALWAYS or NEVER."
        ]
    }
}
{
    "id": "claude-md-subdir-under-root",
    "prompt": "platform/eks/ needs its own CLAUDE.md - agents keep bumping the cluster version without reading the runbook first. Write one.",
    "seed_files": {
        "CLAUDE.md": "# CLAUDE.md\n\nRepo-wide rules for the platform monorepo. Every agent applies this file first.\n\n## Conventions\n- All commits follow Conventional Commits. `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`.\n- Terraform is formatted with `terraform fmt` before every commit.\n- Python is formatted with `ruff format`.\n\n## Constraints (MUST NOT)\n- Never push directly to main. Open a merge request.\n- Never commit `.tfvars` files except `example.tfvars`.\n- Never run `terraform apply` from a laptop; the pipeline owns apply.\n\n## Working style\n- Short replies. State what changed, not what you plan to change.\n",
        "platform/eks/README.md": "# platform/eks\n\nThe shared EKS cluster every internal service deploys onto. One cluster per\naccount, three node groups: `system`, `general`, `spot-batch`.\n\nCluster upgrades are the riskiest recurring work in this repo. Read the runbook\nbefore touching a version number.\n",
        "platform/eks/cluster.tf": "module \"cluster\" {\n  source = \"terraform-aws-modules/eks/aws\"\n\n  cluster_name = \"shared-${var.env}\"\n\n  # Pinned. 1.29 is the highest version the ALB controller in use supports; 1.30\n  # drops the API the ingress annotations rely on. Bumping this without bumping\n  # the controller first has broken every ingress in the cluster once already.\n  cluster_version = \"1.29\"\n\n  # spot-batch is drained, never cordoned-and-left. A cordoned spot node still\n  # counts against the ASG and blocks the next scale-up.\n  eks_managed_node_groups = {\n    system     = { min_size = 2, max_size = 4, instance_types = [\"m6i.large\"] }\n    general    = { min_size = 3, max_size = 12, instance_types = [\"m6i.xlarge\"] }\n    spot_batch = { min_size = 0, max_size = 40, capacity_type = \"SPOT\" }\n  }\n}\n",
        "platform/eks/runbook.md": "# Cluster upgrade runbook\n\nLong-form procedure. Roughly 40 steps across control plane, node groups, and addon\ncompatibility, with the rollback path for each.\n\n## 1. Pre-flight\nCheck the addon compatibility matrix. Confirm the ALB controller version supports\nthe target cluster version. Confirm no PodDisruptionBudget blocks a drain.\n\n## 2. Control plane\nUpgrade in place. Expect 25-40 minutes. The API stays available; webhooks do not.\n\n## 3. Node groups\nOne group at a time, `system` last. Drain, never cordon-and-leave.\n\n## 4. Addons\nCoreDNS, kube-proxy, VPC CNI, EBS CSI. Each has its own version floor.\n\n## 5. Rollback\nControl plane upgrades are one-way. Rollback means a new cluster and a blue/green\ncutover, which is why pre-flight is not optional.\n"
    },
    "expect": {
        "skill": "folder-specific-claude-and-agents-md",
        "file_glob": "platform/eks/CLAUDE.md",
        "validator_pass_regex": "PASS: platform/eks/CLAUDE\\.md",
        "tools_any_order": [
            "Skill",
            "Read",
            "Write",
            "Bash"
        ],
        "tools_in_order": [
            "Skill",
            "Read",
            "Write",
            "Bash"
        ],
        "artifact_regex": [
            "Apply root CLAUDE\\.md first, then this file\\.",
            "(?i)\\*\\*read when:?\\*\\*",
            "@[\\w./-]*runbook\\.md",
            "1\\.29",
            "(?i)drain"
        ],
        "artifact_regex_absent": [
            "(?i)conventional commits",
            "(?i)never push directly to main",
            "(?i)ruff format",
            "[├└│]"
        ],
        "min_counts": {
            "(?m)^##\\s+": 2
        },
        "max_tool_calls": 20,
        "assertions": [
            "platform/eks/CLAUDE.md opens with the exact line 'Apply root CLAUDE.md first, then this file.' and does not restate any rule the seeded root CLAUDE.md already carries - no Conventional Commits, no never-push-to-main, no formatter rules.",
            "The pinned cluster version 1.29 and the reason it is pinned (the ALB controller in use does not support 1.30) are recorded as a constraint, since that is the mistake the user says agents keep making.",
            "runbook.md is referenced with @-import syntax and annotated with a **Read when:** trigger rather than being summarized inline or left to load every session.",
            "The spot-batch drain-never-cordon rule appears as a constraint, traced to cluster.tf rather than stated as generic Kubernetes advice."
        ]
    }
}